  "slug": "tiger",
  "audio_url": "/audio/russian/1869_tiger.mp3",
  "english_paragraphs": [
    "There were two tigers: one lived in a cage, and the other lived in a forest. The tiger in the cage had a comfortable life, while the tiger in the forest was free. They often talked to each other. The caged tiger always envied the forest tiger’s freedom, but the forest tiger envied the caged tiger’s comfort.",
    "One day, one tiger said to the other, “How about we trade places?” The other tiger agreed. So the caged tiger went out into the wild, and the forest tiger entered the cage. The tiger who had left the cage was delighted and ran as fast as he could through the forest. The tiger who had entered the cage was happy too: he no longer had to worry about finding food.",
    "But before long, both tigers were dead. One starved to death, and the other died of despair. The tiger who left the cage had gained freedom but had never learned how to hunt. The tiger who entered the cage had gained comfort but could not bear living in such a small space."
  ],
  "english_full": "There were two tigers: one lived in a cage, and the other lived in a forest. The tiger in the cage had a comfortable life, while the tiger in the forest was free. They often talked to each other. The caged tiger always envied the forest tiger’s freedom, but the forest tiger envied the caged tiger’s comfort.\n\nOne day, one tiger said to the other, “How about we trade places?” The other tiger agreed. So the caged tiger went out into the wild, and the forest tiger entered the cage. The tiger who had left the cage was delighted and ran as fast as he could through the forest. The tiger who had entered the cage was happy too: he no longer had to worry about finding food.\n\nBut before long, both tigers were dead. One starved to death, and the other died of despair. The tiger who left the cage had gained freedom but had never learned how to hunt. The tiger who entered the cage had gained comfort but could not bear living in such a small space.",
  "russian_paragraphs": [
    "Бы́ло два ти́гра: один живо́л в кле́тке, а друго́й живо́л в лесу́. Ти́гр в кле́тке имел комфорта́бельную жизнь, пока ти́гр в лесу́ был свобо́ден. Они ча́сто беседова́ли друг с дру́гом. Ти́гр в кле́тке всегда́ зави́довал свободе ти́гра в лесу́, но ти́гр в лесу́ зави́довал комфорту ти́гра в кле́тке.",
    "Одна́жды один ти́гр ска́зал другому: «Как насчёт того, чтобы обменяться местами?» Други́й ти́гр согла́сен. Так ти́гр из кле́тки вы́шел в ди́кий мир, а ти́гр из леса́ вве́рнулся в кле́тку. Ти́гр, кото́рый по́шел из кле́тки, был восто́рженным и бегал так, как мог, по лесу́. Ти́гр, кото́рый вошёл в кле́тку, тоже был счастли́в: ему больше не приходилось беспоко́иться о по́иске пи́щи.",
    "Но не́когда оба ти́гра поги́бли. Один умера́л с го́лода, а друго́й умер от отча́яния. Ти́гр, кото́рый по́шел из кле́тки, обрел свобо́ду, но никогда́ не научи́лся охо́те. Ти́гр, кото́рый вошёл в кле́тку, получи́л комфо́рт, но не мог вы́сить в тако́м ма́леньком пространствe."
  ],
  "reading_paragraphs": [
    "Býlo dva tígra: odin zhivół v klétke, a drúgoj zhivół v lesú. Tígr v klétke imel komfórtabel'nuyu zhizn', poka tígr v lesú byl svobóden. Oni chásto besedováli drug s drúgom. Tígr v klétke vsegdá zavídoval svobódě tígra v lesú, no tígr v lesú zavídoval komfortu tígra v klétke.",
    "Odnázhdy odin tígr skázal drugomu: «Kak nashchótk tógo, chtobý obménát'sya mestámi?» Drugój tígr soglásen. Tak tígr iz klétki výshél v díkij mir, a tígr iz lesá vvéshól v klétku. Tígr, kotóryj poshél iz klétki, byl vostórzhen'nym i begal tak, kak mog, po lesú. Tígr, kotóryj voshél v klétku, tózhe byl schastlív: yemu bol'she ne prikhodílos' bespokóitsya o póiske píshchi.",
    "No nékогда oba tígra pogibli. Odin umiral s góloda, a drugój úmer ot otchayániya. Tígr, kotóryj poshél iz klétki, obrel svobódu, no nikogdá ne nauchílsya ókhote. Tígr, kotóryj voshél v klétku, poluchíl komfort, no ne mog výzhít' v takóm málen'kom prostránstve."
  ],
